WHY THIS VARIANT (queue "Row 2")
  Row 1 (coro-dlf, PASS = not reproduced) flooded ~48.6 M DLF frames across the stack link at 1G line rate and
  neither CPU saw them (sdma ~24 pps per member throughout); no `coroipcs ... flow control` line appeared.
  corosync is the VCS cluster messaging and coroipcs flow control is its IPC back-pressure, so the hypothesis
  here is CPU-bound traffic crossing the stack: frames the switch must punt to the CPU, entering on the BACKUP
  member (handled on the MASTER). The stack still runs the reporter's config flash:/coro-repro.cfg; its only L3
  interface is vlan1000 10.38.29.15/27 (ports 1.0.9/1.0.24/2.0.9, all down). The injection ports are moved into
  VLAN 1000 (running-only) so vlan1000 comes up and to-me traffic exists.
  Expected: FAIL (= reproduced) if any `coroipcs ... flow control` line appears under CPU-bound traffic;
  PASS (= not reproduced) only WITH proof the CPU was loaded (sdma deltas, `show cpu`) and terminal monitor
  live on both consoles.

